# Intent: The unit stays usable when the hub is not. (1) Wi-Fi power save is NONE while the websocket is down, and an idle unit with the hub up uses MIN_MODEM instead of MAX_MODEM; PERFORMANCE while speaking is unchanged. (2) A tap or the wake word no longer blocks the main task: OpenAudioChannel waits 400 ms instead of 10 s and the caller shows a calm Can't reach Home bubble, a doubtful face and a short tone for three seconds, then goes idle. (3) The reconnect task caps its backoff at 30 s, logs every attempt and pushes a wifi event (state, wifi, rssi, attempt, error, next_ms, took_ms). (4) After 10 s without the hub the ring shows a dim steady amber in place of dark and the bubble says Offline; both clear when the socket is back. A colour asked for on the unit (a ringing timer) still shows.
# Placement: unit (the unit must keep responding with the hub or Wi-Fi down)
# Upstream: main/application.cc, main/application.h, main/protocols/websocket_protocol.{cc,h} of the xiaozhi-esp32 tree (MIT); firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan.cc, hal_bridge.h, hal/hal_io_expander.cpp (MIT)
